{"node_id": "short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024_2_HY_025", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0030"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0030_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "Opposite page: Katherine\nSekaran 1984 is on the left; Julie\nSkarran 2024 is on the right", "semantic_text": "Opposite page: Katherine Sekaran 1984 is on the left; Julie Skarran 2024 is on the right", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0030_geometry", "bbox": [630, 920, 730, 960], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0030"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_236/hybrid/short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024/page_0002/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024_2_HY_026", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0034"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0034_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "It's easy to think of a new year as a blank page we're eager to\nfill- either with the things we didn't get around to last year, or\nwith the ways we can undo last year's mistakes. But this year,\nsince taking the helm at Getty, I have a different kind of to-do\nlist, one that connects to our institutional mission.", "semantic_text": "It's easy to think of a new year as a blank page we're eager to fill- either with the things we didn't get around to last year, or with the ways we can undo last year's mistakes. But this year, since taking the helm at Getty, I have a different kind of to-do list, one that connects to our institutional mission.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0034_geometry", "bbox": [864, 663, 1205, 744], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0034"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_236/hybrid/short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024/page_0002/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024_2_HY_027", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0035", "D0036"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0035_F001", "D0036_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "First on the agenda: the idea of generosity. Getty has been\nphilanthropic since its inception. Following J. Paul Getty's\nvision, early leaders set out to serve all facets of the art world,\nincluding research, display, conservation, publishing, grants, and\neducation. Since the creation of our philanthropy program (the\nGetty Foundation) in 1984, $530 million in grants has supported\npeople across the world and fellow art institutions here in LA.\nJust through our upcoming 2024 iteration of Pacific Standard\nTime (PST Art: Art & Science Collide), we will support some 60\nexhibitions and numerous programs to the tune of roughly $20\nmillion. Our international work has benefited 180 countries on\nall seven continents (yes, even Antarctica)—and has supported\nthe emergence of our disciplines as more inclusive, accessible,\nand comprehensive. Collaborations with other institutions,\nmeanwhile, have created such groundbreaking exhibitions as\nAncient Sculptures: India Egypt Assyria Greece Rome (see p.5),\nwhich just launched at the Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Vastu\nSanghalahya museum in Mumbai.", "semantic_text": "First on the agenda: the idea of generosity. Getty has been philanthropic since its inception. Following J. Paul Getty's vision, early leaders set out to serve all facets of the art world, including research, display, conservation, publishing, grants, and education. Since the creation of our philanthropy program (the Getty Foundation) in 1984, $530 million in grants has supported people across the world and fellow art institutions here in LA. Just through our upcoming 2024 iteration of Pacific Standard Time (PST Art: Art & Science Collide), we will support some 60 exhibitions and numerous programs to the tune of roughly $20 million. Our international work has benefited 180 countries on all seven continents (yes, even Antarctica)—and has supported the emergence of our disciplines as more inclusive, accessible,\nand comprehensive. Collaborations with other institutions, meanwhile, have created such groundbreaking exhibitions as Ancient Sculptures: India Egypt Assyria Greece Rome (see p.5), which just launched at the Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj Vastu Sanghalahya museum in Mumbai.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0035_geometry", "bbox": [863, 744, 1205, 954], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0035"}, {"member_id": "D0036_geometry", "bbox": [1216, 98, 1555, 179], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0036"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_236/hybrid/short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024/page_0002/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024_2_HY_028", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0037"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0037_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "But what about outright generosity? I'd like Getty to be\nknown for sharing: sharing its expertise, its collections, its\nknowledge, and yes—also for sharing its wealth. One early step in\ndoing this has come about through rethinking the Getty Medal.\nFor 10 years the Medal has celebrated stars of the art world—\nartists, philanthropists, institutional leaders, and scholars who\nhave changed the field for the better. We've honored them each\nyear at a gala dinner that, if the one I attended is anything to go\nby, is memorable for its glam factor. But what if we toned down\nthe fanciness and instead used some of the money to create a\nfund honorees could direct as a grant from Getty to a nonprofit\nof their choosing? Starting in 2024, this is the approach we will\nbe taking: we've renamed the award the Getty Prize and will\nfocus each year on one honoree rather than two or three. Thus\nwe will continue the tradition started by Jim Cuno when he\ninvented the Getty Medal but will amp it up by placing gener-\nosity at its very heart.", "semantic_text": "But what about outright generosity? I'd like Getty to be known for sharing: sharing its expertise, its collections, its knowledge, and yes—also for sharing its wealth. One early step in doing this has come about through rethinking the Getty Medal. For 10 years the Medal has celebrated stars of the art world— artists, philanthropists, institutional leaders, and scholars who have changed the field for the better. We've honored them each year at a gala dinner that, if the one I attended is anything to go by, is memorable for its glam factor. But what if we toned down the fanciness and instead used some of the money to create a fund honorees could direct as a grant from Getty to a nonprofit of their choosing? Starting in 2024, this is the approach we will be taking: we've renamed the award the Getty Prize and will focus each year on one honoree rather than two or three. Thus we will continue the tradition started by Jim Cuno when he invented the Getty Medal but will amp it up by placing gener-osity at its very heart.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0037_geometry", "bbox": [1216, 179, 1556, 454], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0037"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_236/hybrid/short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024/page_0002/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024_2_HY_029", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0038"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0038_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "We've just chosen the first Getty Prize recipient: Mark\nBradford, an LA-based abstract artist who will soon choose a\nnonprofit to support (see the story on p. 4). Mark is an excep-\ntional artist whose work sheds light on societal issues and\ncaptivates audiences here in LA and well beyond. A Getty Prize\nworking committee comprised of a small group of staff and\ntrustees unanimously selected him from an impressive list of\nnominees. How wonderful that we can enable him to support\nthe people and projects important to him. At the core of the\nGetty Prize relaunch is the idea that Getty needs perspectives\nother than its own. Mark is helping to bring one, in drawing our\nattention, and that of the world, to the important work done by\nhis selected nonprofit.", "semantic_text": "We've just chosen the first Getty Prize recipient: Mark Bradford, an LA-based abstract artist who will soon choose a nonprofit to support (see the story on p. 4). Mark is an excep-tional artist whose work sheds light on societal issues and captivates audiences here in LA and well beyond. A Getty Prize working committee comprised of a small group of staff and trustees unanimously selected him from an impressive list of nominees. How wonderful that we can enable him to support the people and projects important to him. At the core of the Getty Prize relaunch is the idea that Getty needs perspectives other than its own. Mark is helping to bring one, in drawing our attention, and that of the world, to the important work done by his selected nonprofit.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0038_geometry", "bbox": [1216, 454, 1556, 665], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0038"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_236/hybrid/short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024/page_0002/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024_2_HY_030", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0039"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0039_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "Of course we very much hope that our collaborations with\nMark might well continue—as has happened with Getty Medal-\nists Ed Ruscha and Frank Gehry, whose archives we've been\nsharing through our far-reaching websites 12 Sunsets: Explor-\ning Ed Ruscha's Archive and Sculpting Harmony, wherein Frank\ntells us how he and his team designed Walt Disney Concert Hall.", "semantic_text": "Of course we very much hope that our collaborations with Mark might well continue—as has happened with Getty Medal-ists Ed Ruscha and Frank Gehry, whose archives we've been sharing through our far-reaching websites 12 Sunsets: Explor-ing Ed Ruscha's Archive and Sculpting Harmony, wherein Frank tells us how he and his team designed Walt Disney Concert Hall.", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0039_geometry", "bbox": [1216, 665, 1556, 763], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0039"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_236/hybrid/short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024/page_0002/decisions.json"}
{"node_id": "short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024_2_HY_031", "node_type": "evidence", "status": "HYBRID_SHADOW_CANDIDATE", "unit_type": "TEXT", "source_atom_ids": ["D0040"], "source_fragment_ids": ["D0040_F001"], "source_visual_bundle_ids": [], "plain_text": "I hope it's now on your own new year's list to check out these\nvarious websites, along with that of Mark's chosen organization.\nAnd I hope you'll also find a way to \"pay it forward\" yourself, as\nwe've done with the Getty Prize. Celebrating the important work\nof a third entity by celebrating the accomplishment of our Prize\nwinner feels really good—even nicer than being directly in the\nspotlight ourselves. Thank you, Mark—and here's to generosity!", "semantic_text": "I hope it's now on your own new year's list to check out these various websites, along with that of Mark's chosen organization. And I hope you'll also find a way to \"pay it forward\" yourself, as we've done with the Getty Prize. Celebrating the important work of a third entity by celebrating the accomplishment of our Prize winner feels really good—even nicer than being directly in the spotlight ourselves. Thank you, Mark—and here's to generosity!", "visual_description": null, "geometry_members": [{"member_id": "D0040_geometry", "bbox": [1216, 763, 1556, 876], "bbox_source": "dolphin_v2_resized_image_pixels", "source_atom_id": "D0040"}], "native_visual_components": [], "production_modified": false, "visual_description_status": "UNVERIFIED_RETRIEVAL_HINT", "node_policy": "bounded-v2", "scoring_mode": "embedding_geometry", "hybrid_model_decision_file": "/hkfs/home/project/hk-project-p0025545/dv3352/Project/remote_runs/node-first-realpdf-20261118/output/nodes_prepared_incremental_non_nasa_after_all_parse_20261119/batch_236/hybrid/short_014_getty_magazine_winter_2024/page_0002/decisions.json"}
